<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladislaus III, Duke of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1222">1222</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Vladislaus Henry, Vladislav Jindřich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladislaus Henry, a Přemyslid prince, was briefly Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> in 1197 as Vladislaus III before giving up the throne to his brother Ottokar I in return for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>. As Margrave of Moravia from 1197 until his death in 1222 he united the former Moravian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanages</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a>, ending their separate princely lines and tying Moravia more closely to the Bohemian crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vladislaus-iii-duke-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Vladislaus III, Duke of Bohemia" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: August Sedláček · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PecetVladislavaJindricha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
